# Prefer `gh issue view` / `gh pr view` over `gh api`

When reading GitHub issues or PRs, prefer high-level `gh` commands over `gh api`:

- Use `gh issue view`, `gh pr view`, `gh pr diff`, `gh pr checks`, `gh issue list`, etc. first.
- Prefer `--json` / `-q` on those commands when you need structured fields.
- Only use `gh api` when a dedicated subcommand cannot do the job (mutations that require REST/GraphQL, endpoints with no `gh` wrapper, etc.).

**Why:** `gh issue view` and `gh pr view` (and similar view/list subcommands) have open permissions and do not need user approval. Raw `gh api` calls usually do, which slows the loop.
